xnu 0270: put the touch report rate on the fps line, and name the scan rates

The UI's frame rate follows the digitizer, not the renderer: SpringBoard redraws
once per touch event, so a part that answers four reports a second turns a drag
into four steps, and no amount of compositor work fixes that. Two numbers were
missing to tell it apart from a slow renderer, so the fps line now carries
`poll N/s` (report-thread wakeups) and `ev N/s` (events handed to the HID side)
beside `touch`/`rep`, and the IC info pass logs the scan rates the part is
configured with -- the idle rate is what a drag is stuck at if it never leaves
it.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/mondrian_touch.c b/bsd/dev/mondrian_touch.c
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_touch.c
